[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m programs, enumerating the branch space, and building the differential suite in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/tests/differential.rs` (34 tests).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How it was verified
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - C: `cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && cmake --build .`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   -> `c_src/build/driver`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Rust: `cd translation && cargo build --release`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   -> `translation/target/release/driver`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Comparison: both binaries are spawned as subprocesses, fed the same bytes on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   stdin, and stdout / stderr / exit status are compared. The Rust code is never
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   linked as a library.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - Beyond the committed tests, roughly 3,000 further inputs were compared
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ad hoc: random binary blobs of 0-30 bytes, a numeric sweep from -3000 to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   3000, and every integer from 0 to 120. Zero mismatches.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What the C program branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `main()` contains only three decisions, and `data` (an `int`) drives two of them:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. `fgets(inputBuffer, 14, stdin) != NULL` - success, or the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `"fgets() failed."` path with `data` left at its initializer `-1`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. `data < 100` - `strncpy(dest, source, data); dest[data] = '\0';`, or the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    copy skipped entirely so `dest` keeps its all-zero initializer.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. `printLine`'s `line != NULL` - unreachable as false; both call sites in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `main()` pass non-null buffers.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Resulting input classes, all covered:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | Class | Example input | Observable result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | EOF before any byte | empty stdin, `/dev/null`, closed fd 0 | `data == -1`, killed by SIGSEGV, stdout empty |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `data == 0` | `0`, `\n`, `abc`, `   ` | one `\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `0 < data < 100` | `5`, `98` | `data` `A`s then `\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `data == 99` (max in range) | `99` | 99 `A`s then `\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `data >= 100` | `100`, `1000`, `2147483647` | copy skipped, one `\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `data < 0` | `-1`, `-100`, `-2147483648` | killed by SIGSEGV, stdout empty |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `atoi` truncation to `int` | `4294967296` -> 0, `4294967396` -> 100, `2147483648` -> `INT_MIN` | follows the wrap |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `fgets` 13-byte limit | `999999999999999` -> `9999999999999` | 14th byte onward dropped |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `fgets` stops at newline | `7\n50\n` | second line never read |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Divergence candidates that were checked and already correct
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These are the places a translation would most plausibly have gone wrong. Each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m was confirmed to match; none required a fix.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Negative length passed to `strncpy` must crash, not clamp.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `data` is a signed `int` implicitly converted to `size_t`, so `data == -1`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    becomes `SIZE_MAX`. glibc copies the 99 `A`s from `source` and then pads with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    NUL bytes until it walks off the 100-byte stack buffer. Both programs are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    killed by SIGSEGV (signal 11, shell status 139). A translation that clamped
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the count, saturated it, or panicked would have shown up here: a Rust panic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    exits 101 and writes to stderr, whereas the C writes nothing to stderr.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`"fgets() failed."` is printed but never observed when stdout is a pipe.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    glibc fully buffers stdout when it is not a terminal, so the message is still
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    in the buffer when SIGSEGV kills the process, and is lost. The C program's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    stdout is therefore *empty* on this path despite the `printf`. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    translation reproduces this by buffering and deliberately not flushing before
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the fault.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. **The same path *does* emit the message when stdout is a terminal.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Under line buffering the `printf` reaches the fd before the crash. Driving
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    both binaries through a pty (`script -q -c ... /dev/null`) confirms both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    print `fgets() failed.\r\n` and then die. This is the one case that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    distinguishes a correct buffering model from a translation that either always
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    flushes or never flushes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. **`atoi` is `(int)strtol(s, NULL, 10)`, not a checked parse.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Leading whitespace skipped, one optional sign, conversion stops at the first
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    non-digit, no error on trailing junk, and the `long` result is *truncated* to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `int`. So `50abc` -> 50, `abc50` -> 0, `0x1F` -> 0, `0.9` -> 0,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `4294967396` -> 100, `2147483648` -> `INT_MIN` (which then crashes).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    A translation using `str::parse::<i32>()` would fail on all of these.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. **`fgets` with a 14-byte buffer keeps at most 13 payload bytes, and does not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    read across newlines.** `00000000000009` truncates to `0000000000000`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`data == 0`), and in `7\n50\n` the `50` is never consumed. This is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `scanf`-vs-`fgets` distinction; a `read_to_string`-based translation would
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    have consumed the whole stream.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. **`strncpy` does not NUL-terminate when the count is consumed, and pads when
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the source is shorter.** Only reachable benignly here because `dest` is
